            <ArticleTitle>Answers to Clinical Questions in the Primary Care Management of People with Obesity: Communication and Patient Self-Management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S5-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Body weight is a sensitive subject for most people; this statement is particularly true for people who are overweight or have obesity, because social stigmatization is common not only in society but also in the health care setting. Health care providers are often unaware of their own biases toward patients with obesity. Here's how to improve your communication and support of these patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
